Gauss law, symmetry and what flux does not determine (@em-gauss: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @electromagnetism, #source "../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q", #source "../sources/Eletromagnetismo-Classico-Volume-I-IFRN.lingua#r_612RCJJJDNWD62YYPE9410HHVQ", #electromagnetism "../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Energy-power-and-capacity.lingua#r_0EE7P9TMJK8SRVCVM1M7K61RAR") { r_6EEA738C5T368TVSQ82K6J5QBY
**Read:** [University Physics Volume 2 — OpenStax](../sources/University-Physics-Volume-2.lingua#r_5JQ0CPQ0RNJNVH175Y9V305J5Q), chapter 6 in full; [Eletromagnetismo Clássico, Volume I — Tibério Magno de Lima Alves](../sources/Eletromagnetismo-Classico-Volume-I-IFRN.lingua#r_612RCJJJDNWD62YYPE9410HHVQ), Gauss law and electrostatic symmetry sections.

Gauss's law states ∮E·n dA = Q_enclosed/ε₀ in vacuum. It constrains a total flux for any closed surface. It determines a field magnitude directly only when symmetry or other independent information supplies the remaining spatial structure.

Derive the fields of a spherical charge distribution, an infinite line and an infinite sheet. State why the tangential components cancel or why the chosen field magnitude is constant on the relevant part of the Gaussian surface. A zero enclosed charge means zero net flux, not zero field. An externally generated uniform field through a closed cube is an immediate counterexample.

Use a thin pillbox across a charged sheet to derive the normal E jump σ/ε₀. For a finite sheet, identify where the infinite-sheet approximation is plausible and where fringing matters. Reconstruct the differential form from shrinking volumes and identify the distributional meaning for ideal point/surface charges. Solve at least one nonsymmetric source by integration to show why a clever Gaussian surface alone cannot replace missing symmetry.

**Continue:** [Energy, power, capacity, and a production denominator](../../../inquiry/quantitative-literacy/practice/Energy-power-and-capacity.lingua#r_0EE7P9TMJK8SRVCVM1M7K61RAR).

